\section{Functions}{
\itemize{
\item \code{trial_report()}: BCTU trial report Word output format

An \code{\link[rmarkdown:word_document]{rmarkdown::word_document()}} output format for BCTU trial reports. It
uses the bundled BCTU \code{reference.docx} (styles, running header and footer,
logo) and the bundled \code{title_page.lua} pandoc filter, which builds the
title page from YAML metadata, inserts an optional Word table of contents,
turns \verb{::: landscape} fenced divs into landscape sections, numbers
figure and table captions above their content, and styles a \verb{::: footnote}
fenced div placed straight after a table as that table's footnote block.
Declare the format in the YAML header of an \code{.Rmd} and render it with
\code{\link[rmarkdown:render]{rmarkdown::render()}}:
\preformatted{
output:
  bctu::trial_report: default
}
\code{theme} in the YAML header restyles the document. Its keys are the
elements of \code{\link[=report_theme]{report_theme()}}, which inherit from one another (set
\code{colour.accent} and every rule, border and header fill follows; set one
of them to override just that), and every element not given keeps the
template default: UoB gold accents, Arial at 11 pt, the title acronym in
Times New Roman. The same colours and fonts can be changed afterwards in
Word under Design.
\preformatted{
theme:
  colour.accent: "C59A00"
  table.header.fill: "F3EBCC"
  font.body: "Arial"
  font.size: 11
}
The title-page filter reads these YAML keys (pandoc's own \code{title},
\code{author} and \code{date} are not used):
\itemize{
\item \code{trial-short-name}, \code{trial-long-name}, \code{trial-registration},
\code{report-type}, \code{report-subtype}: the title-page lines;
\item \code{metadata}: a list of rows for the table at the foot of the title page.
Each item is \code{Label: value}, where the value is a string, a list of
strings, a \verb{\{name, role\}} map, or a list of such maps;
\item \code{include-toc} (\code{true}/\code{false}) and \code{toc-depth} (default 3): the Word
table of contents;
\item \code{trial-logo}: path to an image (PNG, GIF or JPEG; relative paths are
read from the Rmd's folder) placed in the title-page header opposite the
BCTU logo: right-aligned to the same margin and centred on it
vertically. It is scaled to fit \code{trial-logo-width} by
\code{trial-logo-height} (defaults \code{"2in"} by \code{"1in"}, units in, cm, mm or
pt) with its aspect ratio kept, and is never taller than the BCTU logo;
\item \code{confidential}: text for a confidentiality page, centred on a page of
its own after the title page. Omit the key for no such page.
In RStudio, \strong{File > New File > R Markdown > From Template > "BCTU trial
report (Word)"} opens a skeleton with every key filled in.
}

\item \code{repair_report_docx()}: Repair a rendered trial report docx

Applied by \code{\link[=trial_report]{trial_report()}} to the file pandoc has just written. It binds
the title-page headers and footers to the relationship ids pandoc chose,
widens full-width images inside landscape sections to the landscape text
width, sets each autofit table's width (see \code{\link[=render_table]{render_table()}}), keeps each caption with the start of its table, drops the empty
final section a report ends in when its last content is landscape,
applies any theme given, fills the table of contents with the headings
(see \code{populate_toc()}), writes the running header and footer field
results (see \code{fill_running_fields()}), removes pandoc's
update-fields-on-open setting so Word opens the file without a prompt,
and stamps the package version and template into the document properties
(see \code{stamp_provenance()}).

\item \code{report_provenance()}: Read the provenance stamp of a rendered report

\item \code{report_styles()}: The styles a report template offers

Every paragraph, character and table style in the template's reference
document, by the name pandoc's \code{custom-style} attribute uses. In an Rmd,
\verb{::: \{custom-style="Footnote Block Text"\}} wraps paragraphs in a
paragraph style and \verb{[text]\{custom-style="Section Number"\}} applies a
